     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Considering that the project just started on 15 Augustus 2022 and Inception Workshop on 5 and 6 October 2022, it is too soon to register the results of activities in the fields.
2. To ensure the progress and performance, the project developed Operational Community-Grant Guidelines and Grievance Mechanism, and Standard Operational Finance for SGP-7 Implementation.
3. The project launched a Grievance Mechanism aiming at providing easily accessible procedure for grantee partners to address any issues or concerns they may have regarding the implementation of activities and the management of grant funds. 
4. Conducted Call for Proposal for Developing Landscape Strategies for the four-target landscapes. The Secretariat published a request for proposals on October 7-25, 2022 inviting national consortiums of NGOs/ Educational institutions/ Research institutions to participate in the preparation and development of Strategic Landscape Documents in four locations. PMU received three proposals at the time. However, only one proposal was considered for the National Steering Committee member evaluation process. The proposal passed to the next stage because it met the criteria, namely that the activities were carried out by more than one institution and they would work in four geographic locations. 
5. Draft of Memorandum of Agreement (MoA) between YBUL (as the Implementing Partner) and the selected institution to conduct Landscape Strategies was prepared for the signatures of both parties. The selected institution is expected to start developing the Strategic Landscape Document immediately after signing the MoA in the end of 2022.
6. Prepared Baseline Assessment Report: the Secretariat (PMU) prepared baseline assessment reports for the project landscapes in Central Java and South Sulawesi, including updated information on priority areas for biodiversity conservation, rehabilitation of degraded land, priorities for renewable and clean energy among local communities, opportunities for introducing or enhancing alternative livelihoods for local people, and incorporating gender-responsive processes.
7. Participated in one SGP-UCP global workshop: PMU attended the online SGP-UCP global workshop on November 9, 2022. The keynote speaker was Sri Lanka&#x2019;s National Coordinator. She shared her experiences as well as the learning process of GEF SGP-6 management in that country.
8. Selected and organized the National Steering Committee SGP-7 Members&#x2019; First and Second Meetings. The NSC member selection process started from July to September 2022. As many as 11 NSC members are determined from the process with a composition of government representatives, UNDP, YBUL, private sector, research/educational institutions, NGOs, other donors, journalists, etc. NSC first meeting was held on 22 September 2022 and the second meeting was on 11 November 2022 (for proposal screening). 
9. Organized Project Inception Workshop: PMU organized two days the project inception workshop on 5 and 6 October 2022. In this workshop PMU together with UNDP CO, NSC members, and other stakeholders reviewed the project institutional arrangement, multi-year work plan, project results framework, gender analysis and gender action plan, stakeholder engagement plan, social and environmental screening procedure, global environmental contribution, etc.
10. Prepared, submitted and uploaded Project Inception Workshop Report into UNDP-GEF PIMS database on 16 November 2022.</narrative>
